  "scope": "The shared inspect_dispatch_recovery pass admits each original request, validates identity/image, reads original signed counters and owned optional retry error, then checks delivery attempts, retry counters/history, lazy retry-error admission and completion parity in the original order. The real SQLite loader delegates inside its existing checkpoint finalizer. Native SQL/header reads, bounded codecs, schema and lease integrity, authentic requests, global graph/audit checks and atomic commit stay adapter-owned. No counter reset, clamping, new dispatch, fuel charge, replay permission or complete native durable VM is introduced. Frozen comparisons preserve exact faults and original metadata/effect/dispatch/group/branch tables. Late SQLite refusal blocks snapshot and watermark publication until repaired. Standalone consumers cover numeric boundaries, move-only local owners, unsized hosts, native error provenance/redaction, every reached hook unwind, final cleanup and late-proof/commit failure. Native callbacks/destructors are trusted; arbitrary side effects cannot be rolled back.",
